dsh-bestthink-standard
======================

This project is a port and composition of an upstream MIT-licensed research
preset for DeepSeek Harness, plus the official `standard` agent preset as a
base composition. The MIT license of this project covers the new composition,
the extensions, and the fixes added on top of the ported files; the ported
code and the official base retain their original copyrights below.

Ported sources (MIT)
--------------------

1. `dsh-anchored-standard` — first-turn trajectory anchoring
   (first-request tool-surface narrowing, output-budget cap and release,
   injected-context stripping).
   Repository: https://github.com/xiaobright/dsh-anchored-standard
   License: MIT
   Ported files:
     - preset/tool-bootstrap.mjs (mechanisms and configuration names;
       extended with the first-turn quick-action guide, configurable
       suppressed-context sources, and promotionSignal exports)

2. `dsh-router-standard` — task-aware reasoning-mode routing
   (spec/react/weak behavior bands, persona selection, near-field guidance).
   Repository: https://github.com/yjh051108/dsh-router-standard
   License: MIT
   Status: the task-router implementation was ported, measured, and removed
   (see README "Development history"); no code from this repository is
   retained. Its near-field guidance insight (a fixed message injected right
   after the user message, never into the system prompt) influenced the
   first-turn quick-action guide wording and placement.

Official DeepSeek Harness base (see repository license)
--------------------------------------------------------

`preset/agent.cordis.yml` is derived from the official `standard` agent
preset shipped with DeepSeek Harness 0.1.0-rc.5 / commit 47f9438
(https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness), with the persona row
replaced by the minimal-aligned row (`complete: true` +
`includeRuntimeContext: false`) and the bootstrap row prepended. The
official copyright and license of the DeepSeek Harness repository apply to
the derived rows.

All ported files retain their original comments and configuration names so
upstream diffs stay readable.
